<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vardan Mamikonian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 387–451</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Saint Vardan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vardan Mamikonian was an Armenian military leader of the Mamikonian noble house who led the Christian rising against the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-ii">Yazdegerd II</a>'s attempt to impose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoroastrianism">Zoroastrianism</a>. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr">Battle of Avarayr</a> in 451, but the resistance he began eventually secured religious freedom for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. He is a saint of the Armenian Church and a national hero of Armenia.</p></div>
